    "body": "## Motivation\n`_handle_embedding_request` validates the input length but, on failure, queues the request without finishing it. A prompt that fits the context length but not the KV pool is then never scheduled and never answered: the client hangs until its timeout. The generate path already aborts in this case.\n\n## Modifications\n- `scheduler.py`: `req.set_finish_with_abort(error_msg)` when `validate_input_length` fails.\n- New regression test `test_embedding_length_validation.py` (`--max-total-tokens 1000`, 1500-token input): expects HTTP 400, then a normal request still succeeds.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nNo model-output change. New test: 2/2 pass with the fix; without it both fail with `ReadTimeout`. `test_embedding_models::test_prefill_logits` passes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nN/A (error path only).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41800300909](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800300909)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41800300876](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800300876)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41800300920](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800300920)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
